%[text] %[text:anchor:M_64b5] ## Introduction to Generative AI
%[text] %[text:anchor:M_8fcf] Generative AI (GenAI) [models](internal:M_2185) are a class of artificial intelligence systems that generate new content such as text, images, music, code, and video. This is achieved by learning patterns from large amounts of existing data. Many GenAI models used for text-based tasks are powered by large language models (LLMs), which are trained on vast collections of text from sources such as books, websites, code, and conversations. During training, these learned patterns are encoded in the model’s parameters. An LLM is a specialized type of GenAI model designed to understand, generate, and process human language, making it an essential component behind many text‑based GenAI capabilities. [AI Chatbots](internal:M_6c26) are a common application layer through which users interact with GenAI models and LLMs. The following image illustrates this hierarchy from application to model level.
%[text]{"align":"center"} ![GenAI Hierarchy](text:image:0c04)
%[text] %[text:anchor:M_4c8d] You've likely already used AI Chatbots like OpenAI's ChatGPT™, Microsoft Copilot™, Google Gemini, or Anthropic's Claude™. Each of these Chatbots can interact with their own various LLMs (e.g. ChatGPT with GPT-3.5, GPT-4, etc.). LLMs vary based on speed, accuracy, creativity, and capability for complex reasoning. GenAI is only the first step into the possibilities of current forms of AI. Consider some of the other types of AI that may occupy this space and how they compare to GenAI:
%[text:table]{"columnWidths":[107,521,574]}
%[text] | <p align="center">**AI Option**</p> | <p align="center">**Purpose**</p> | <p align="center">**Example**</p> |
%[text] | --- | --- | --- |
%[text] | <p align="center">**Generative AI**</p> | <p align="center">To create new content in response to user input (Text, images, code, videos, etc.).</p> | <p align="center">It creates a generic email in response to a user prompt</p> |
%[text] | <p align="center">**AI Agent**</p> | <p align="center">A single semi-autonomous AI system designed to pursue goals and take actions on a user's behalf.</p> | <p align="center"> It creates an email by deciding what information to retrieve from external sources and incorporates that data into the message</p> |
%[text] | <p align="center">**Agentic AI**</p> | <p align="center">One or more AI Agents that autonomously plan, coordinate, and carry out complex multi-step tasks and workflows end-to-end.</p> | <p align="center">Autonomously manages email workflow by deciding what information or data is needed for the email, generating the email, determining the recipients, sending the email, monitoring the responses, and adaptively providing follow-up responses based on replies</p> |
%[text:table]
%[text] 
%[text] %[text:anchor:TMP_4170] Agentic AI builds on generative AI by adding autonomy, planning, and action, using LLMs to pursue goals and shifting AI agents from reactive to proactive actions.
%[text] 
%[text] %[text:anchor:M_35a2] ![Exercise icon](text:image:34c3) **Exercise 1.** I have a variety of AI options at my disposal and want to use them to help me solve a problem. I want to autonomously book the cheapest nonstop flight from Boston to London next Friday, and returning on a Wednesday. I have a preference for aisle seats and want to use my airline miles for booking. In addition, I want to arrange transportation upon arrival and have the summarized options sent to my email. Which AI option would be best suited in creating this travel plan?
ExerciseSol1("Select an answer..."); %[control:dropdown:53e3]{"position":[14,35]}
%%
%[text] %[text:anchor:M_0a8c] ### GenAI Literacy
%[text] %[text:anchor:M_352d] GenAI literacy encompasses the skills and competencies needed to understand, evaluate, use, and ethically manage AI tools, including the LLMs on which they are based. Having GenAI as a useful skill requires understanding its capabilities and limitations. Another important skill for using GenAI is creating effective prompts.
%[text] %[text:anchor:M_8876] #### Prompting
%[text] %[text:anchor:M_5be4] Using well-written prompts is key to producing the desired results from an LLM. They can range from being [simple](internal:M_51e9) to very [complex](internal:M_9240). They help to define the task, context, and constraints which help to determine the accuracy of the LLMs output. When writing a prompt, you should consider a few questions:
%[text] - What are the best practices for creating prompts?
%[text] - Did the prompt you created generated the results you expected?
%[text] - Should you trust the results? If not, how can you improve them? \
%[text] ![lightbulb mark](text:image:8363) **Note**. For more practice with prompting, check out the [CopilotForLearners.m](file:CopilotForLearners.m) script.
%[text] #### Capabilities
%[text] GenAI provides a wide array of benefits in day-to-day tasks that can increase productivity or efficiency. Here are a few notable ones:
%[text] - Producing drafts (emails, papers, etc.)
%[text] - Summarizing (datasets, text, meeting notes)
%[text] - Creating content (images, videos)
%[text] - Writing code and debugging support
%[text] - Brainstorming ideas \
%[text] %[text:anchor:M_0232] ![Warning symbol](text:image:96c1) **Warning**. It should be stated with emphasis that you should <u>**ALWAYS**</u> validate the output of the LLM before using the information provided in your own work. For example, verifying sources of the information provided or validating that the code produced can be executed with no failures.
%[text] #### Limitations
%[text] While GenAI and LLMs can provide significant benefits, their underlying limitations make it essential to understand how and when to use them appropriately within a given context. For example, you could ask an LLM to compute the product of two numbers. You may get multiple and/or wrong answers. Why? Here are some reasons that could this could happen:
%[text] - Base LLMs are limited to knowledge from their training cutoff (Access to other software)
%[text] %[text:anchor:M_7761] - LLMs will not give you the same output every time (Stochastic results)
%[text] - Outputs from LLMs may have mistakes or be completely false ([Hallucination](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hallucination_(artificial_intelligence))) \
%[text] Additionally, there are other considerations regarding GenAI that may have societal impacts:
%[text] - Lack of diverse training data for LLMs can skew model outputs (Information Bias)
%[text] - Loss or leakage of personal information (Data privacy) \
%[text] Let's look at an example of how using GenAI may have an impact on a situation:
  %[control:button:299f]{"position":[1,2]}
displayFormula(["'You own an ice cream company that has attracted a lot of customers to its subscription program. '";"'The program promises two free cones a month as long as you remain subscribed. '";"'As a business owner, you want to find a way to leverage GenAI to make it easier to reach your subscriber base. '";"'You choose the free open source AI agent online and provide it with your customer data so that it can send emails on your behalf. '";"'The agent prioritized sending emails to those who have been subscribed the longest and not the newest subscribers. '";"'Not only did this streamline processes for the business but it reduced overhead as well.'"])
%%
%[text] ![Exercise icon](text:image:89d0) **Exercise 2.** Based on the scenario from above, identify the following areas where GenAI may create concerns for your company. Please select all that apply and click the **Submit Answers** button below.
ExerciseSol2(...
    A = false, ... %[control:checkbox:029c]{"position":[9,14]}
    B = false, ... %[control:checkbox:2ee8]{"position":[9,14]}
    C = false, ... %[control:checkbox:53c6]{"position":[9,14]}
    D = false); %[control:checkbox:5211]{"position":[9,14]}
  %[control:button:1caf]{"position":[1,2]}
