%[text] %[text:anchor:H_ADAD31AE] ## Glossary
%[text] %[text:anchor:M_2185] **Model** - A complex, computer-based algorithm trained on vast datasets to understand, interpret, and generate human language, code, and other content. [(↑ Return to Text)](internal:M_8fcf)
%[text] %[text:anchor:M_6c26] **AI Chatbot/Assistant** - User-facing interface powered by an LLM. [(↑ Return to Text)](internal:M_64b5)
%[text] %[text:anchor:M_51e9] **Simple Prompt** - A prompt that follows a clear command structure of an action, topic, and constraint. [(↑ Return to Text)](internal:M_5be4)
%[text] %[text:anchor:M_9240] **Complex Prompt** - A detailed, multi-part instruction designed to guide the model through intricate tasks by providing persona, context, constraints, and specific output formatting [(↑ Return to Text)](internal:M_5be4)
%[text] %[text:anchor:M_093b] **Tool** - A separate product or service (API) called by an LLM. A tool can also be seen as a callable function. [(↑ Return to Text)](internal:M_8be1)
%[text] %[text:anchor:M_681a] **API** - (Application Programming Interface) A set of rules and protocols that allows different software applications to communicate, exchange data, and share functionality. [(↑ Return to Text)](internal:M_8159)
%[text] %[text:anchor:M_3599] **MCP** -  An open standard for AI applications to connect to external tools and data. [(↑ Return to Text)](internal:M_8de7)
